  "narration": "The bolt jumps in its keeper and the cellar door bangs outward. Hobb comes up the steps like a thrown sack, all elbows and teeth, and his fist finds your ribs before you have your feet set.\n\n\"You'll hang for this, you and the reeve both! *Both* of you!\" he screams, spit flying.\n\nYou take the blow, catch his collar and drive him sideways into the doorpost. The whole frame of the Reeve's Hall shivers. Hobb sags against the wood, gasping.\n\nCasimir Krasnov has not moved from behind his table. \"Put him back down there,\" he says flatly. \"Gently or otherwise. I've no stomach for a hanging tonight.\"\n\nVarya Volkov is already at your side, steadying your arm. \"You're bleeding. Sit a moment \u2014 I've linen in my pack, and you've earned a mug.\"\n\nOlek Tarasch grins through his split lip and claps your shoulder. \"Told you he was the one, didn't I? I'd follow you up any road in this valley, sellsword.\""
 },
