  "narration": "Casimir counts the coins out one by one, as if each costs him a tooth, and slides the stack across the table.\n\n\"Thirty-five. As agreed.\" A pause. \"The hall's thanks, too, for what they're worth.\"\n\nVarya binds your side with clean linen while Olek fetches the mug she promised. The rain keeps on at the shutters."
